                <pb facs="0867" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg743"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    121.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">rumor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[From the Monitor Republicano, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1880-10-24">October 24,
                        1880</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>For three days the following rumor has been in circulation:</p>
                <p>The American minister sent a note to the government asking permission for
                    American troops to cross the frontier in pursuit of Indians, stating that if
                    this permission should be refused they would pass anyhow.</p>
            </div>
